WEBVTT

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:30.476
so your want self
won't get sucked back in,

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:32.386
which is what Peggy does for Margaret,

00:14:32.410 --> 00:14:36.506
who loves Twitter and sometimes posts
random questions that pop up.

00:14:36.530 --> 00:14:41.500
MA: For instance, I put up a picture
of a weird mushroom,

00:14:41.524 --> 00:14:42.746
and said, what is this?

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:44.223
Because I couldn't find it.

00:14:44.247 --> 00:14:45.462
(Adam laughs)

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:47.406
AG: When you're tweeting,

00:14:47.430 --> 00:14:49.737
how often does that happen
while you're writing?

00:14:49.761 --> 00:14:53.040
Do you actually interrupt yourself
or get distracted by social media?

00:14:53.064 --> 00:14:54.806
MA: No, no. No, no way, no.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.093
I might get distracted

00:14:56.117 --> 00:15:00.376
before I take the plunge
into the writing burrow